Hello,

After working on and off for a year or so, I have a Biodiversity Patch
ready. The original goal was to flesh out some monster classes that seemed
under-represented (eg: leprechaun).  In the Biodiversity Patch, I have
added monsters so that no class has less than three monster types (l is
now leprechauns, brownies, and pookas).  The new monsters generally have
new characteristics, some more complex than others. Some old monsters have
been altered, and one (Quantum Mechanic) has been retro-altered (they have
names again, but in a new, clever way).

There is also some environmental support, such as trees growing from
acorns, skies that behave differently (eg: no peircers) than cielings, and
more variation on statues. This means I also tinkered with the lev utils.

And there are some unrelated changes that got swept up in the whole thing
(midi for musical notes on win23, engravings made of light).

Some of the coding is less than ideal (especially the older stuff), but
(except for the lev utils) everything is easily disabled/enabled in
config.h.

To use this patch, I assume that you know how to compiler nethack and have
done so, and can use patch.
http://userfs.cec.wustl.edu/~naw1/nh_patches.html

I can put a win32 binary on that page, if anyone would like to try it out
without compiling.

I would appreciate feedback so that I can balance the monsters.

Thanks,
